Translation patch: `From<Duration> for Value`

Change: `(f64::from(nanos) / 1000_f64).round() as u32` becomes `(nanos + 500) / 1000` in `u32`, where `nanos` is `subsec_nanos()`.
Why: Aeneas rejects the float constant ("Improperly typed constant value"); float arithmetic is not modelled.
Behaviour: Identical for every `nanos < 10^9` (all values of `subsec_nanos`). Write `nanos = 1000 k + r` with `k < 10^6`, `r < 1000`. If `r = 500`, `k + 0.5` is exactly representable, so the division is exact and `round` (half away from zero) gives `k + 1`. Otherwise the exact quotient is at least `0.001` away from `k + 0.5`, far more than the f64 rounding error at this magnitude (below `2^-32`), so `round` gives `k` for `r < 500` and `k + 1` for `r > 500`. In all cases this is `(nanos + 500) / 1000`, which is at most `10^6` (so `as u32` was exact) and `nanos + 500` does not overflow.

